---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../site";
import { encodedEmailLink } from "../lib/content";
import { PERSON_ID } from "../lib/seo";
---
<Base title="About" type="profile" description="Corneliu Croitoru, AI Architect & Product Builder: 20+ years of software engineering, 7 at AWS, and what I believe about building with AI." schema={[{ "@type": "ProfilePage", "@id": `${SITE.url}/about/#profile`, url: `${SITE.url}/about/`, mainEntity: { "@id": PERSON_ID } }]}>
  <main class="wrap narrow">
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I'm Corneliu. I have been shipping software since 2003: Java first, then PHP, Python and TypeScript. I spent 7 years at AWS as a Solutions Architect, then as a Senior GenAI Prototyping Architect, building more than 30 prototypes with customers across EMEA, GenAI-only after ChatGPT. Since September 2025 I have been Staff GenAI Solutions Architect at Betclic.</p>
      <p>I also co-founded two travel products, both live: <a href="https://streetlensapp.com">StreetLens</a>, GPS audio guides, and <a href="https://www.backfrommytrip.com">Back From My Trip</a>, trip reports with one verdict. I co-created <a href="https://github.com/2fastlabs/agent-squad">Agent Squad</a> and a handful of MCP servers.</p>

      <h2>Cloud</h2>
      <p>Before GenAI, the cloud. Seven years at AWS: serverless, edge, media streaming, security, for hundreds of customers. AWS Certified Solutions Architect Professional and Security Specialty. Everything I build still runs serverless: StreetLens and Back From My Trip on Supabase Edge Functions, this site as static pages.</p>

      <h2>How I build with AI</h2>
      <p>The model reads. Code decides.</p>
      <p>Most problems still want a query, a rule or a cron job, not a prompt. When a model does belong, the pattern matters more than the prompt: an agent that sees the data but never writes the reply, a pipeline that extracts facts before it narrates, a second model as reviewer instead of author.</p>
      <p>A model is a fast pair of hands, not an architect. It writes code, docs and tests under my direction, and nothing I can't explain gets shipped.</p>

      <h2>Speaking</h2>
      <p>AWS re:Invent, AWS Summits, the AWS GenAI Loft at Station F, and AWS podcasts in English and French. The list, with links, is on my <a href="/cv/">CV</a>.</p>

      <h2>Photography</h2>
      <p>I photograph the places I travel to. The series are <a href="/photography/">here</a>.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Paris. Write to me at <Fragment set:html={encodedEmailLink(SITE.email)} />, or find me on <a href={SITE.links.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>. Code is on <a href={SITE.links.github}>GitHub</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: calc(var(--read) + 2 * var(--gutter)); }
  .prose { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.65; }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 1.1em; }
  .prose h2 { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 22px; margin: 1.8em 0 0.5em; }
  .prose a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; }
</style>
